<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9106" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">col-luctor</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conl-</span></b> ), āri, v.
		n., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
				struggle</i>, <i>contend</i>, <i>wrestle with</i> (post-Aug. and rare); constr. with <i>cum aliquo</i>, <i>alicui</i>, or <i>absol.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedonibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Ham. 523</span></i>
			.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>, <i><span class="en">Just. 13, 8, 8</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 129</span></i>.—<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum agro,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					1, 3, 9</span></i>
			; cf.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum solo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					27, 2, 2, § 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cum petulantiā morbi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Gell.
					12, 5, 9</span></i>
			.</div>
